From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Local build <local@localhost>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] EXP overview: keep the views between openings
 (KWIN_OVERVIEW_VIEW_CACHE=0 turns it off)

Each opening of the Overview built its Qt Quick scene again: on the B50 desktop (a desktop CPU) ~20 ms of the
compositor's main thread before the first frame - two runs of ~10 ms after QuickSceneEffect::startInternal, the first
change ~34 ms after the last one before it (bench/ab/kde_maximize_trace_1104.sh kmt7/kmt8, KMT_STALL=1, Meta+W); in the
window-operations test the first opening of a pass showed 42-66 ms without a change (dgk4). QuickSceneEffect has had
opt-in view caching since !8998 (hidden views release their GL resources and render nothing), meant for this effect,
whose port was left out of the merge. The overview clears its search text at each activation, and its window and desktop
models follow the workspace while hidden.
---
diff --git a/src/plugins/overview/overvieweffect.cpp b/src/plugins/overview/overvieweffect.cpp
index d50cbae..9be1977 100644
--- a/src/plugins/overview/overvieweffect.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/overview/overvieweffect.cpp
@@ -172,6 +172,13 @@ OverviewEffect::OverviewEffect()
     });
     delegate->loadFromModule(QStringLiteral("org.kde.kwin.overview"), QStringLiteral("Main"), QQmlComponent::Asynchronous);
     setDelegate(delegate);
+
+    // EXP (2026-11-04): the overview's views kept between openings (QuickSceneEffect's opt-in view caching, upstream
+    // !8998, which meant to port this effect and did not): each opening built the whole Qt Quick scene again - ~20 ms
+    // of the compositor's main thread on a desktop CPU before the first frame (bench/ab/kde_maximize_trace_1104.sh with
+    // KMT_STALL=1, Meta+W). Hidden views release their GL resources and render nothing; KWIN_OVERVIEW_VIEW_CACHE=0
+    // builds them at each opening as before.
+    setViewCachingEnabled(qEnvironmentVariable("KWIN_OVERVIEW_VIEW_CACHE") != QLatin1String("0"));
 }
 
 OverviewEffect::~OverviewEffect()
